# ptygate configuration template.
# Copy this file to .env and set values there, or set them in the hosting
# panel's environment settings. Panel-provided environment variables take
# precedence; this file is filled in at startup and is ignored by git.

# ─── Required setup ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PORT — the one public port the hosting panel routes to this server.
# Required in this file only if the panel does not already set PORT or
# SERVER_PORT for the process. Use your panel's allocated port.
#
# TERMINAL_TOKEN — the ptygate login token for /login, minimum 16
# characters.
# DEFAULT BEHAVIOR: if empty, a new random token is generated on every
# start and printed once in the server log ("Access token: ..."). Set a
# fixed value to keep the same login across restarts.
#
# DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_TRUSTED_HOSTS — comma-separated hostnames that
# browsers use to reach the DeepSeek Harness page under /ai/, for
# example: mohamedalsayed.ccwu.cc,mohamedalsayed.ccwu.cc:443
# This list is passed to Harness's own hostname check. It is separate
# from ptygate's login and does not grant anyone access by itself.
# DEFAULT BEHAVIOR: if empty, only the internal loopback address is
# trusted and /ai/ does not load under a public hostname.
PORT=
TERMINAL_TOKEN=
DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_TRUSTED_HOSTS=

# ─── Optional — variable=default ─────────────────────────────────────

# HOST=0.0.0.0
# Bind address. Keep 0.0.0.0 in hosted containers so the panel proxy
# can route the public port. Change only for local use.

# ALLOW_PRIVATE_ONLY=0
# 1 restricts even the login page to allowlisted source IPs.
# DEFAULT: 0 (any source IP is allowed to attempt login; the token
# still protects every route).

# ALLOWED_IPS=
# Comma-separated IPs/CIDRs used when ALLOW_PRIVATE_ONLY=1.
# DEFAULT: empty.

# SHELL_BIN=/bin/bash
# Shell used for terminal sessions.
# DEFAULT: the value of the process SHELL environment variable,
# otherwise /bin/bash.

# COOKIE_SECURE=0
# 1 marks ptygate's login session cookie Secure, which browsers only
# accept over HTTPS. Set 1 once the browser-facing URL is HTTPS, for
# example behind a Cloudflare/TLS proxy. Your current domain
# (https://mohamedalsayed.ccwu.cc) should use 1.
# DEFAULT: 0 (correct while the browser-facing URL is plain HTTP).

# ─── DeepSeek Harness model access — optional ────────────────────────

# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Optional. Read directly by the Harness process (ptygate only passes
# environment through). Equivalent to entering a DeepSeek API key in
# the /ai/ UI under Settings → Models, which is the documented setup
# path. DEFAULT: unset (no model account configured).
